{
  "_comment": "L2 clarify-gate contract. The gate is deterministic (no model), it fires on ~17% of the ffmpeg corpus in the native runtime, and nothing previously proved Python's equivalent fires on the same rows. Given (utterance, plan, registry) both runtimes must produce the same post-gate payload: the plan with chain intermediates bound to their producer, or a single clarify step. Consumed by python/core/tests/test_clarify_gate_parity.py and `clarify_gate_parity_cases` in native/crates/knaif-core/tests/parity.rs.",
  "_stage": "The stage is `link_chain_intermediates -> hallucinated-filename guard`, in that order. Python composes it in CommandAgent.infer; native in knaif_core::apply_clarify_gate. Comparing either half alone would violate Rule 2. A case may declare `sandbox_files`: the filenames present in the agent's sandbox at gate time. The guard exempts a value whose STEM the user named when that value is one of those files, so both runtimes must be given the same listing to agree. Absent means an empty sandbox — nothing can be confirmed, and the strict substring rule applies. The link stage includes forward-threading: a later reference to a single-source producer's source is rewritten onto its output only when the user named that source at most once (whole-filename, case-insensitive), and never onto a file of a different kind. A case may declare `file_kinds` exactly as a skill.yaml does (kind -> extensions); absent means no kinds. See docs/plans/2026-09-23-chain-source-threading.md.",
  "_expected_values": "Produced by the reference runtime (Python CommandAgent._link_chain_intermediates then ._hallucinated_filename). DO NOT regenerate to make a failing test pass.",
  "_coverage": {
    "ubuntu": "CI",
    "windows": "local",
    "macos": "unexercised"
  },
  "registries": {
    "demo": "resize_video:\n  description: \"Resize a video.\"\n  required_args: [inputs]\n  optional_args: [height, output]\nstrip_audio:\n  description: \"Remove the audio track.\"\n  required_args: [inputs]\n  optional_args: [output]\nconcat_video:\n  description: \"Join several videos.\"\n  required_args: [inputs]\n  optional_args: [output]\ninspect_video:\n  description: \"Report a video's properties.\"\n  required_args: [inputs]\nwatermark_video:\n  description: \"Stamp a watermark on a video.\"\n  required_args: [inputs]\n  arg_schemas:\n    output: {type: string, help: \"where to write it\"}\nclarify:\n  description: \"Ask the user one question.\"\n  required_args: [question]\nreject:\n  description: \"Refuse the request.\"\n  required_args: [reason]\ndone:\n  description: \"Nothing to do.\"\n",
    "chain": "strip_audio:\n  description: \"Remove the audio track.\"\n  required_args: [inputs]\n  optional_args: [output]\ntrim_video:\n  description: \"Cut a time range.\"\n  required_args: [input]\n  optional_args: [start, end, output]\nreverse_video:\n  description: \"Play a video backwards.\"\n  required_args: [inputs]\n  optional_args: [output]\nconcat_video:\n  description: \"Join several videos.\"\n  required_args: [inputs]\n  optional_args: [output]\nconvert_video:\n  description: \"Change a video's container.\"\n  required_args: [inputs]\n  optional_args: [container, output]\ncompress_video:\n  description: \"Make a video smaller.\"\n  required_args: [inputs]\n  optional_args: [output]\ncreate_thumbnail:\n  description: \"Save one frame as an image.\"\n  required_args: [inputs]\n  optional_args: [output]\ninspect_video:\n  description: \"Report a video's properties.\"\n  required_args: [inputs]\nunlock_pdf:\n  description: \"Remove a PDF's password.\"\n  required_args: [input, password]\n  optional_args: [output]\nfind_in_document:\n  description: \"Search a document for text.\"\n  required_args: [input, query]\nclarify:\n  description: \"Ask the user one question.\"\n  required_args: [question]\nreject:\n  description: \"Refuse the request.\"\n  required_args: [reason]\ndone:\n  description: \"Nothing to do.\"\n"
