    {
      "name": "named_stem_resolving_to_a_real_file_is_not_hallucinated",
      "why": "People name files the way they say them. 'downscale clip_4k to 1920x1080' names the stem; the model supplies clip_4k.mp4, the file that is actually there. Testing the full filename as a substring of the utterance overrode that correct plan with a clarify and cost the T6a control arm eight utterances across seven slices (evals/runs/2026-09-12_t6a-control_success/report.md).",
      "registry": "demo",
      "utterance": "downscale clip_4k to 1920x1080",
      "sandbox_files": [
        "clip.mp4",
        "clip_4k.mp4",
        "clip_no_audio.mp4"
      ],
      "plan": {
        "plan": [
